UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53735329703540
DTSTART:20260822T132000Z
DTEND:20260822T183000Z
DESCRIPTION:Rotating sessions are a key part of Orientation where students 
 move through a series of small-group workshops and activities on different
  topics. \n\n \n\nMorning Meeting \n\nCanon Lounge\n\nAll students should 
 meet at Canon Lounge by 9:20 AM\, where your Orientation Week Leader (OWL)
  will greet you and walk you to your first rotating session. This ensures 
 a smooth start to the day as you begin exploring a variety of Orientation 
 activities and campus resources. \n\n \n\nInclusive Excellence / Spiritual
  Life at Warren Wilson College\n\nMeet Outside\, Ransom House\n\nJoin the 
 offices of Inclusive Excellence and Spiritual Life for an informative sess
 ion on Warren Wilson College’s vision for fostering inclusion and how yo
 u can contribute to this vital work on campus. You’ll learn about the va
 rious areas across campus that offer programming and support systems\, hel
 ping students explore and celebrate their faith\, spirituality\, race\, et
 hnicity\, sexuality\, and gender identity.\n\n \n\nWarren Wilson Working L
 ands Talk\n\nMeet Outside\, Blacksmith Cabin\n\nWarren Wilson College is n
 ationally recognized for its commitment to environmental sustainability\, 
 and Dr. Dave Ellum will highlight a new initiative\, the Center for Workin
 g Lands. This session will explore programs and opportunities focused on c
 limate and agriculture\, food justice\, land and habitat conservation\, ec
 ological landscape design\, and sustainability leadership. Additionally\, 
 you'll learn crucial bear safety strategies\, including how to prevent enc
 ounters\, what to do if you spot a bear\, and how to respect wildlife whil
 e enjoying the natural beauty of our campus and surrounding areas.\n\n \n\
 nCenter for Experiential Learning & Careers \n\nCanon Lounge  \n\nGet read
 y to explore the CELC at Warren Wilson College! This session is a great op
 portunity for students to discover the wide range of resources available i
 n the Center for Experiential Learning and Careers\, including the Career 
 Services\, Internship and Research Offices\, and Academic Support programs
 . Join us to learn how these offices can help you gain hands-on experience
 \, connect with professional opportunities\, and make the most of your col
 lege journey. \n\n \n\nWellbeing (Consent+) \n\nBoon 110  \n\nGet ready fo
 r an engaging and interactive session on wellbeing and consent! This sessi
 on gives students the chance to explore important topics through discussio
 ns\, activities\, and real-life scenarios\, empowering you to make informe
 d decisions\, build healthy relationships\, and take charge of your person
 al wellbeing in a supportive environment.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:New Student Orientation Rotating Sessions
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/new-student-orientatio
 n-rotating-sessions
END:VEVENT
