DESCRIPTION:Mapping Home\n\n \n\nElizabeth Holden Gallery’s exhibition Ma
 pping Home will be on view at Warren Wilson College from August 27th to Oc
 tober 3rd\, 2026.\n\n \n\nThe notion of home takes on a whole new meaning 
 after a climate disaster like Hurricane Helene.  Home is a place of reflec
 tion\, home is near and far\, home provides shelter\, home is lost and fou
 nd\, and home is created when a community comes together. In this exhibiti
 on we will collectively map our idea of home alongside the WWC community\,
  our Swannanoa Valley neighbors\, and WWC Alumni. Featured artists include
  Galen Bernard\, Carolina Corona\, Annie Hall\, Sonia Norris\, Kaye Savage
 \, Tissica Schoch\, Jess Self\,  Carson Whitmore\, Rebecca Williams and a 
 community installation organized by Melanie Wilder. \n\n \n\nWe are inviti
 ng community participation for this exhibition through fiber workshops\, t
 hrough art responses and through fundraising for our local nonprofit organ
 ization Swannanoa Communities Together\, which provides rent assistance pr
 ograms for residents of Swannanoa.  \n\n \n\nThe opening reception for the
  exhibition is on Thursday\, August 27th from 4:30-6:00 PM.  The Elizabeth
  Holden Gallery is open M-F\, 10-4pm and most Saturdays 1-4pm.\n\n \n\nThi
 s exhibition is in partnership with the Fiber Arts Crew\, Swannanoa Artist
  Collective\, Climate Action Now\, WWC Art & Craft Department and is suppo
 rted by the Windgate Foundation and Educating for Character Initiative Gra
 nt from the Lily Foundation.
GEO:35.611409;-82.441422
LOCATION:Holden Arts Building \, Elizabeth Holden Gallery 
SUMMARY:Mapping Home: Opening Reception
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/mapping-home-opening-r
 eception
CATEGORIES:Social
END:VEVENT
